    {
      "unit": "U11",
      "test": "harness/rigs/hostkey-persist.sh — first use on a fresh target, none after"
    }
  ],
  "description": "When opening the session's connection accepted a target host key on first use, the create response carries hostkey {fingerprint, first_use: true}, and every surface shows the fingerprint and asks for acknowledgement before it attaches: accept, warn, record. A reused or already-known connection carries no hostkey. First use happens once per target, so this cannot be reproduced on demand against a standing core: only a provider's test and the harness's host-key rig grade it; the C3 capture of the same event is graded from artefacts (hostkey-event).",
  "corpus": [
    "decision 5.18",
    "spine plan.md §5 5.18"
  ],
